This machine's forwarding rules (PengyOS). Empty unless this box routes.

/etc/nftables.conf includes every *.nft file here at the end of the forward
chain of `table inet pengyos`, whose policy is drop. Each file holds
forward-chain rule statements, written by hand, e.g. for a router:

    iifname { "lan0", "wg0" } oifname { "wan0", "lan0" } accept
    iifname "wan0" oifname "lan0" meta nfproto ipv6 drop

The chain already accepts established/related traffic and anything a DNAT rule
redirected (`ct status dnat accept`), so port forwards need nothing here; the
DNAT rule in ../table/ is what decides what is exposed.

Check before reloading, then reload (never `nft flush ruleset`: that also
deletes rootful podman's tables):

    sudo nft -c -f /etc/nftables.conf && sudo systemctl reload nftables

Files under /etc survive OS updates, and adding them never shadows the image's
/etc/nftables.conf. An example router bundle is in
/usr/share/pengyos/examples/router/ on the Server.
